Falsifies `capability::reap_is_permitted_only_to_the_supervising_rendezvous`.

The defect: the fall-through arm of `reap_decision` authorizes any corpse, not only
one this rendezvous supervises. Written the way it would actually arrive, as a
"reaping is harmless, it only collects the dead" simplification: the liveness test
is kept, so every hand-written test about a live stranger still passes, and only the
supervision relationship is dropped. That is the whole claim gone, and
with it the property that a supervisor cannot collect (and so free the pages of)
another supervisor's child.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(supervising_rendezvous, Some(invoked), "reaped through the wrong
rendezvous")` in the `Reap::Permitted` arm, on any `supervising_rendezvous` that is `None` or
names some other rendezvous while `dead` holds.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
index dcd2cbb5..be92a85b 100644
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -206,6 +206,7 @@ pub const fn reap_decision(fault_ep: Option<u64>, invoked_ep: u64, dead: bool) -
                 Reap::StillAlive
             }
         }
+        _ if dead => Reap::Permitted,
         _ => Reap::NotSupervised,
     }
